// Reference query. Not deployed in any employer environment.
// Title: Microsoft Entra control-plane change (Tier 0 role assignment, Conditional Access or named location change, domain federation or sync change, cross-tenant access change) or a vendor PIM-for-Groups activation outside expected hours
// Status: untested template
// ATT&CK: T1098.003 (Account Manipulation: Additional Cloud Roles), T1556.009 (Modify Authentication Process: Conditional Access Policies), T1556.007 (Modify Authentication Process: Hybrid Identity), T1484.002 (Domain or Tenant Policy Modification: Trust Modification), T1199 (Trusted Relationship), T1078.004 (Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts); ATT&CK v19.2
// Data sources: Microsoft Sentinel, AuditLogs (Microsoft Entra ID data connector)
// Licensing assumptions: Microsoft Sentinel with the Entra ID connector (scenario A-17); PIM and PIM for Groups audit events require Entra ID P2 (scenario holds P2)
// Rule ID: SN-02 | Platform: Microsoft Sentinel scheduled analytics rule | Suggested severity: High for trust, sync, and policy changes, any assignment or activation of a never-assigned role, and permanent Tier 0 assignments outside PIM; Medium for other Tier 0 role assignments and activations, scoped Tier 0 assignments, and vendor activations
// Tactics: Persistence (TA0003), Privilege Escalation (TA0004), Defense Impairment (TA0112), Initial Access (TA0001)
// Answers: detection-priorities.md item 10 (Priority 2), the cloud half of item 9, and the PIM activation part of item 15; attack-paths.md AP-5 steps 6 to 8 and AP-3 step 3
// Architecture context: PE-IDENTITY (Conditional Access set CA-01 to CA-22), IGA-ENTRA (PIM, PIM for Groups), IDS-SYNC, IDS-PARTNER, the vendor session groups grp-vendor-ehr-session and grp-vendor-biomed-<vendor>-session (03 section 7; flows F-06 and F-07); risk register R-04 and R-05
// Fictional scenario: Contoso Regional Health (fictional). Reference portfolio content.
//
// Purpose
//   After a cloud foothold, durable access comes from changing the control plane: adding a role, editing
//   Conditional Access, trusting a new federation or partner, or flipping directory sync settings. The
//   architecture already says Sentinel alerts on these (03-identity-and-access.md section 4); this is the
//   query behind that statement. It also watches the vendor path (AP-3): a PIM-for-Groups activation of a
//   vendor session group outside the hours vendors normally work.
//
// Logic
//   Activity names come from Microsoft's Entra audit activity reference:
//   - Role changes: "Add member to role", "Add eligible member to role", "Add member to role outside of PIM
//     (permanent)", and the two scoped forms the reference lists, "Add scoped member to role" and "Add
//     member to role scoped over Restricted Management Administrative Unit", matched by a text match on the
//     target resources to the Tier 0 Entra roles in 03-identity-and-access.md section 4 (Global
//     Administrator, Privileged Role Administrator, Privileged Authentication Administrator, Conditional
//     Access Administrator, Security Administrator, Hybrid Identity Administrator, Domain Name
//     Administrator, Intune Administrator, Application Administrator, and Cloud Application
//     Administrator), plus every PIM activation of those roles.
//   - Scope: 03 section 4 places Application Administrator and Cloud Application Administrator in Tier 0
//     when assigned at tenant scope, and treats an assignment scoped to one application that is not Tier 0
//     as Tier 1. The rule does not tell the two apart. Microsoft's role assignment reference records scope
//     as directoryScopeId ("/" for the tenant, "/" followed by an application's object ID for one
//     application), but the audit activity reference lists activity names only, so which activity and
//     which target properties an app-scoped assignment logs is left to the lab (purple-team-plan.md PX-17
//     records both). The rule alerts on an assignment of either role under any activity above, scoped forms
//     included, and an app-scoped assignment to an application that is not Tier 0 is closed against its
//     record.
//   - Never-assigned roles: the same role activities for the roles that 03-identity-and-access.md section 4
//     says are never assigned: Partner Tier1 Support and Partner Tier2 Support (Microsoft's role reference
//     says "Do not use" for both), Windows 365 Administrator, and External Identity Provider
//     Administrator. Any assignment is High.
//   - Policy changes: Conditional Access policy, named location, authentication context, continuous access
//     evaluation, and security defaults activities.
//   - Trust and sync changes: "Set domain authentication", "Set federation settings on domain",
//     "Set DirSyncEnabled flag", "Set DirSync feature", and four of the nine CrossTenantAccessSettings
//     activities in the reference: "Add a partner to cross-tenant access setting", "Update a partner
//     cross-tenant access setting", "Delete partner specific cross-tenant access setting", and "Update the
//     company default cross-tenant access setting".
//   - Vendor activations: "Add member to role completed (PIM activation)" for any vendor session group, EHR
//     or biomedical (VendorSessionGroupPattern), outside ExpectedVendorHoursUtc. The audit activity
//     reference lists this PIM for Groups form under Category GroupManagement, but the rule identifies the
//     row by the group name, not by Category: Microsoft's Graph directoryAudit reference documents category
//     values such as GroupManagement, while its Azure Monitor AuditLogs table reference says Audit is the
//     only supported value.
//   Changes to grp-ca-emergency-access, grp-admins-t0, and grp-admins-t1, and audit activity by or on the
//   emergency access accounts, are SN-07's. SN-02 still alerts on every Conditional Access policy change,
//   including a change to which group a policy targets or excludes (03 sections 3 and 5).
//
// Known false positives
//   - Planned changes by the Conditional Access team; match against change tickets (P-5) before closing.
//   - PIM activations by Tier 0 administrators doing approved work (Tier 0 activation needs approval from
//     one of two named approvers, so the useful question is whether the approval matches a ticket).
//   - Vendor emergencies at night with a Contoso owner's documented approval (the system owner for the EHR
//     vendor, clinical engineering for a biomedical vendor).
//
// Tuning knobs (let statements below)
//   Tier0RolePattern         regular expression of the Tier 0 Entra role names in 03 section 4. The Tier 0
//                            row there also names Defender roles that can run live response on all
//                            devices, Azure roles that can write to the resources hosting Tier 0 managed
//                            identities, and Active Directory Domain Admins and Enterprise Admins. None of
//                            those is an Entra directory role, and this rule does not watch them
//                            (coverage-map.md section 3, item 10).
//   ScopedRoleActivities     the two scoped role activities, labeled separately so the responder checks
//                            the assignment's scope.
//   NeverAssignedRolePattern regular expression of roles the design never assigns (03 section 4).
//   VendorSessionGroupPattern  regular expression for the PIM-for-Groups vendor session groups. 03 section 7
//                              names grp-vendor-ehr-session and one grp-vendor-biomed-<vendor>-session group
//                              per biomedical vendor, all following grp-vendor-*-session, so one pattern
//                              covers both. A group named outside that convention is not matched.
//   ExpectedVendorHoursUtc   start and end hour (UTC) of normal vendor activity.
//
// Response notes
//   Unplanned Tier 0 or trust changes: treat as a suspected Tier 0 compromise and follow the identity
//   compromise playbook's Tier 0 branch from a Tier 0 PAW. An assignment of a never-assigned role has no
//   planned form: remove it and investigate the actor as for an unplanned Tier 0 change. An assignment of
//   Application Administrator or Cloud Application Administrator: confirm its scope against the ticket. At
//   tenant scope it is Tier 0 work under a Tier 0 change record. Scoped to one application, it is Tier 1
//   only when that application is not Tier 0; scoped to a Tier 0 workload identity (the application owner
//   registry, 03 section 6), handle it as an unplanned Tier 0 change, because its holder can add a
//   credential to that application and act as it (03 section 4). A Privileged Authentication
//   Administrator activation that no ticket explains also calls for a review of the credential changes
//   made in the window: SN-07 alerts on any change to the emergency access accounts, but changes to other
//   Tier 0 accounts show only in AuditLogs. Unplanned vendor activation: end the activation,
//   end the broker session in PEP-VENDOR-BROKER, and call the vendor through the contact on file, not one
//   supplied in the session. For a biomedical vendor, tell clinical engineering, which approves those
//   activations (F-07); if the session reaches a device in clinical use, the clinical safety gate applies
//   (playbook decision point D5).
//
// Validation notes
//   Not run against any workspace. Validate in a lab tenant, each change made by an authorized
//   administrator. Role, policy, and trust branches (purple-team-plan.md exercise PX-17): assign a role
//   that Tier0RolePattern lists, edit a report-only Conditional Access policy, and change a federation or
//   cross-tenant access setting. PX-17 gives Privileged Authentication Administrator and Security
//   Administrator runs of their own, assigns Application Administrator scoped to a single lab application
//   and records the activity name and target properties that assignment logs and whether SN-02 alerted,
//   and records an assignment of a privileged role outside both lists as a coverage gap, not a miss. Its
//   never-assigned run exercises the never-assigned branch for each role it assigns; a role in
//   NeverAssignedRolePattern that the lab does not assign stays unexercised. Its exclusion-group and
//   admin-group steps are SN-07's. Vendor activation branch (exercise PX-11): activate PIM for Groups
//   membership in a vendor session group at an off-hours time, once with an EHR group name and once with
//   a biomedical group name, so the pattern is tested on both. Expected telemetry: one AuditLogs row per
//   change, with an OperationName from the RoleActivities, PolicyActivities, or TrustActivities lists
//   below, and "Add member to role completed (PIM activation)" for each vendor activation; record the
//   Category value the lab shows on that row (see Logic).
//
// References
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/monitoring-health/reference-audit-activities
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity/role-based-access-control/permissions-reference
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/rbacapplication-post-roleassignments?view=graph-rest-1.0
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/directoryaudit?view=graph-rest-1.0
//   https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-monitor/reference/tables/auditlogs
//   https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1098/003/
//   https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1556/009/
//   https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1484/002/
//
let LookbackWindow = 1h;
// The Tier 0 Entra roles in 03 section 4
let Tier0RolePattern = @"(?i)(Global Administrator|Privileged Role Administrator|Privileged Authentication Administrator|Conditional Access Administrator|Security Administrator|Hybrid Identity Administrator|Domain Name Administrator|Intune Administrator|Cloud Application Administrator|Application Administrator)";
// Roles the design never assigns (03 section 4): any assignment alerts
let NeverAssignedRolePattern = @"(?i)(Partner Tier1 Support|Partner Tier2 Support|Windows 365 Administrator|External Identity Provider Administrator)";
// The two scoped role activities in the audit activity reference; labeled so the responder checks scope (Logic)
let ScopedRoleActivities = dynamic(["Add scoped member to role", "Add member to role scoped over Restricted Management Administrative Unit"]);
let RoleActivities = dynamic(["Add member to role", "Add eligible member to role", "Add member to role outside of PIM (permanent)",
    "Add member to role completed (PIM activation)", "Add scoped member to role",
    "Add member to role scoped over Restricted Management Administrative Unit"]);
let PolicyActivities = dynamic(["Add Conditional Access policy", "Update Conditional Access policy", "Delete Conditional Access policy",
    "Add named location", "Update named location", "Delete named location", "Add AuthenticationContextClassReference",
    "Update AuthenticationContextClassReference", "Delete AuthenticationContextClassReference", "Update continuous access evaluation",
    "Update security defaults"]);
let TrustActivities = dynamic(["Set domain authentication", "Set federation settings on domain", "Set DirSyncEnabled flag", "Set DirSync feature",
    "Add a partner to cross-tenant access setting", "Update a partner cross-tenant access setting", "Delete partner specific cross-tenant access setting",
    "Update the company default cross-tenant access setting"]);
// Every vendor session group: grp-vendor-ehr-session and grp-vendor-biomed-<vendor>-session (03 section 7)
let VendorSessionGroupPattern = @"(?i)grp-vendor-[a-z0-9-]+-session";
let ExpectedVendorHoursUtc = dynamic([12, 23]);
AuditLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(LookbackWindow)
| where OperationName in~ (RoleActivities) or OperationName in~ (PolicyActivities) or OperationName in~ (TrustActivities)
| extend TargetText = tostring(TargetResources),
         Actor = coalesce(tostring(InitiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName), tostring(InitiatedBy.app.displayName)),
         ActorIP = tostring(InitiatedBy.user.ipAddress),
         HourUtc = datetime_part("hour", TimeGenerated)
| extend ChangeClass = case(
    OperationName in~ (TrustActivities), "Trust or sync change",
    OperationName in~ (PolicyActivities), "Conditional Access or location change",
    OperationName =~ "Add member to role completed (PIM activation)" and TargetText matches regex VendorSessionGroupPattern, "Vendor PIM-for-Groups activation",
    OperationName in~ (RoleActivities) and TargetText matches regex NeverAssignedRolePattern, "Never-assigned role assignment",
    OperationName in~ (ScopedRoleActivities) and TargetText matches regex Tier0RolePattern, "Scoped assignment of a Tier 0 role",
    OperationName in~ (RoleActivities) and TargetText matches regex Tier0RolePattern, "Tier 0 role assignment or activation",
    "")
| where isnotempty(ChangeClass)
| where not(ChangeClass == "Vendor PIM-for-Groups activation" and HourUtc between (toint(ExpectedVendorHoursUtc[0]) .. toint(ExpectedVendorHoursUtc[1])))
| extend SuggestedSeverity = case(
    ChangeClass == "Trust or sync change", "High: federation, domain authentication, sync, or cross-tenant trust changed",
    ChangeClass == "Never-assigned role assignment", "High: a role the design never assigns was assigned or activated (03 section 4)",
    ChangeClass == "Scoped assignment of a Tier 0 role", "Medium: scoped assignment of a Tier 0 role, confirm the scope and the ticket",
    ChangeClass == "Tier 0 role assignment or activation" and OperationName =~ "Add member to role outside of PIM (permanent)", "High: permanent Tier 0 role assigned outside PIM",
    ChangeClass == "Tier 0 role assignment or activation", "Medium: Tier 0 role change or activation, confirm the ticket and approvers",
    ChangeClass == "Conditional Access or location change", "High: Conditional Access or named location changed, confirm the change ticket",
    "Medium: vendor session group activated outside expected hours")
| project TimeGenerated, ChangeClass, SuggestedSeverity, OperationName, Category, Result, Actor, ActorIP, TargetResources, AdditionalDetails, CorrelationId
